## Contact

An individual person at an Account — you sell to people, not logos. `firstName`/`lastName` (computed `name`), base `EmailField`/`PhoneNumberField`, `jobTitle`, `role` enum (decision maker/champion/influencer/user/billing — a label, deliberately NOT color-coded as a lifecycle), `account = linksTo(Account)`.

```ts
import { Contact } from '../contact';
@field decisionMakers = linksToMany(Contact);
```

Linked from Deal.decisionMakers; the Customer 360 view lists an account's contacts by query.

Embedded renders click-to-call and click-to-email as `tel:` and `mailto:` links, in a constant-width slot so rows still align for a contact with no phone. The links stop click propagation, because a consumer commonly wraps the row in its own target and reaching the person should not also open their card.

**Non-goals:** internal people (that's User/Teammate), lead capture (Lead converts INTO a Contact via the Convert Lead command), social profiles, comms history (Activity's job).
